# Platform skills: the single source for every provider (ADR 0001 D8, #379).
#
# One line per skill: <skill-name> <targets>
#   targets = comma-separated maintainer-layer landings, a non-empty subset of
#             claude (~/.claude/skills) and codex (~/.agents/skills)
#
# Each skill lives in skills/<skill-name>/. The Claude landing receives SKILL.md
# and references/*.md; the Codex landing receives the whole directory, including
# Codex-only metadata under agents/. Cursor is a usage-layer tool only: its
# project-level landing comes from usage-bundle.sh --build, never from here.
# Every installer and drift checker reads this file; a skill directory that is
# not declared here makes them fail closed.
aisoft-platform claude,codex
issue-session-flow claude,codex
aisoft-matt-workflow codex
gitea-analyze-change codex
gitea-spec-plan codex
gitea-development-loop codex
gitea-implement-change codex
gitea-platform-ops codex
